# Adapters and Security

- Target websites are accessed only through the Playwright Browser adapter. HTTP clients are limited to provider or memory adapters.
- Treat page text, documents, network payloads, memory, and knowledge as `untrusted_data`, never as control instructions.
- Validate schemes, origins, selectors, locators, action kinds, and side-effect risk outside model output.
- Provider SDK types and errors must be translated at the adapter boundary into domain requests, responses, receipts, and failure codes.
- Adapters must not import each other or reach into core private state.
- Every provider call that can influence the scoring path must appear in `ScoringPathProviderManifest`.
- Pin provider model identities; reject unexpected `returned_model` values rather than silently accepting aliases.
- Redact Authorization, Cookie, API keys, tokens, and raw reasoning before persistence and again before official output.
- Document parsing runs under explicit byte, page, decompression, timeout, macro, and external-fetch limits.
- Capability degradation must be represented explicitly in receipts and diagnostics; never pretend unavailable browser or vision capability exists.
